Q2. What is the difference between Abstraction and
Encapsulation?

Interview Ready Answer

Abstraction

• Hides implementation details.
• Focuses on "What to do".
• Achieved using Abstract Classes and Interfaces.
• Reduces complexity.

Example

You call

paymentService.pay();

You don't know how payment processing works.

------------------------------------------------------------

Encapsulation

• Hides data.
• Controls access to data.
• Achieved using private fields and access modifiers.
• Improves security.

Example

private double balance;

Balance cannot be accessed directly.

It can only be accessed through controlled methods.

